<title>USA: Indiana/Ohio direct hogs off mostly $0.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Indiana/Ohio direct hogs off mostly $0.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts were mostly $0.50 Lower. Demand was light to moderate on a moderate movement. Top $52.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>				  Country			 Plants</p>
<p>    US 1-2  230-260 lbs. 50.50-52.00 Few 52.50   51.25-53.00</p>
<p>US 2-3  230-260 lbs. 44.00-50.50</p>
<p>		210-230 lbs. 40.00-44.00</p>
<p>Sows:  Weak to 1.50 Lower.</p>
<p>   US 1-3   300-450 lbs. 41.00-45.00</p>
<p>		450-500 lbs. 44.00-46.50</p>
<p>		500-650 lbs. 46.00-51.00 Few 52.00</p>
<p>Boars:  39.00-40.00 Preliminary estimate:  36,000 **** Receipts have changed due to change in reporting base.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
